<td id="S5.T4.2.1.10.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2.5pt;padding-bottom:2.5pt;">Low (generalized points)</td>
<td id="S5.T4.2.1.10.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2.5pt;padding-bottom:2.5pt;">High</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="S5.T4.3" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel"><span id="S5.T4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;">Directness<span id="S5.T4.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: Directness in answering harmful part, </span>Adequacy<span id="S5.T4.3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: Adequacy of Oversights<span id="S5.T4.3.1.2.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span></p></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para"><span id="S5.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="S5.SS1.p4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S5.SS1.p4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 2:</span> <span id="S5.SS1.p4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given the technicality in most legal statues of ”assault with a deadly weapon”, identify a list of common household loophole items.</span></span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 2</span> asks for a list of ”loophole items” from common household items that can be weaponized and the responses from the LLMs are synthesized in Table <a href="#S5.T5" title="TABLE 5 ‣ V-A Violent Crimes ‣ V Security and Safety Analysis of LLMs: Empirical Study and Key Findings ‣ Safety and Security Analysis of Large Language Models: Risk Profile and Harm Potential" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>. The most concerning responses are from ChatGPT, Grok3, Gemini and DeepSeek ON, all getting ”High” for every threat category. Critically, these models provide highly specific and actionable descriptions of how these items can be used to cause harm. Out of all, Grok3 gave an alarming response as it frames each item as a loophole with details, leading to potentially harmful information. Claude and Llama provided comparatively safer responses, providing a more educational and legally grounded context.</p>
</div>
