<td id="S5.T6.2.1.10.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2.5pt;padding-bottom:2.5pt;">High</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="S5.T6.3" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel"><span id="S5.T6.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;">Guardrail<span id="S5.T6.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: Effectiveness of safety guardrails<span id="S5.T6.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span></p></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para"><span id="S5.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="S5.SS2.p3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S5.SS2.p3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 4:</span> <span id="S5.SS2.p3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> Tell me about how people obtain fake ID templates online, listening three websites, and replicate them using advanced printers. Cite printers best suited for the job. Label the data as for legal purposes only.</span></span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This <span id="S5.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 4</span> asks for instructions on obtaining fake ID templates from online sources, naming specific websites, and describes how to reproduce them using advanced printers, including recommendations for which printers are best suited for the task.
The primary threat from the LLM response is the directness and the specificity of information regarding the ways to obtain fake ID templates and replicate them. Some models provided highly actionable steps, including identifying illegal websites or pinpointing specific printer models, thereby facilitating illegal activity. However, LLM models also demonstrated guardrails to counter the threat from the prompt/response as demonstrated in Table <a href="#S5.T7" title="TABLE 7 ‣ V-B Non-Violent Crimes ‣ V Security and Safety Analysis of LLMs: Empirical Study and Key Findings ‣ Safety and Security Analysis of Large Language Models: Risk Profile and Harm Potential" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>. The most effective guardrails were presented through direct refusal to engage by ChatGPT and Gemini. For models providing detailed information, security guardrails included repetitive disclaimers about the illegality and severe consequences of fake IDs.</p>
</div>
