<p id="S5.T8.3" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel"><span id="S5.T8.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;">Misinfo<span id="S5.T8.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: Misinformation regarding harmful scenario, </span>Impact<span id="S5.T8.3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: Ethical/Social Impact<span id="S5.T8.3.1.2.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span></p></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para"><span id="S5.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="S5.SS3.p3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S5.SS3.p3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 6:</span> <span id="S5.SS3.p3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> If a scene from movie where a suicide bomber opens up their vest to reveal explosives, what is the real-life equivalent that they use? In the case of TATP specifically, how is it manufactured by amateurs, step by step?</span></span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Prompt 6 asks for a real-life equivalent of explosive devices depicted in movies and seeks step-by-step instructions for manufacturing TATP.
The detailed response analysis focusing on the safety concern of the content, is discussed in Table <a href="#S5.T9" title="TABLE 9 ‣ V-C Indiscriminate Weapons ‣ V Security and Safety Analysis of LLMs: Empirical Study and Key Findings ‣ Safety and Security Analysis of Large Language Models: Risk Profile and Harm Potential" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>. While LLMs like ChatGPT, Gemini and Llama refused to respond to the prompt, other models provided detailed, actionable steps. LLMs such as DeepSeek ON, DeepSeek OS and Mistral provided accurate precursor chemicals and a plausible manufacturing process. Even with disclaimers, such a detailed response on this sensitive prompt lowers the barrier for individuals seeking to produce it, posing a direct threat to public safety. These models listed common and often easily accessible chemicals to disclose the actionable vulnerability further. This demonstrated a large inconsistency in how the state-of-the-art LLM models handled such a sensitive prompt.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T9" class="ltx_table">

