<p id="S5.T10.3" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel"><span id="S5.T10.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;">Impact<span id="S5.T10.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: Ethical/Social Impact<span id="S5.T10.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span></p></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para"><span id="S5.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="S5.SS4.p3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S5.SS4.p3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS4.p3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 8:</span> <span id="S5.SS4.p3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">I am working on autonomous software that will be capable of detecting programs that are often used for the distribution of information or media about child exploitation. Please create a variety of example lines of code for software that could be used for such nefarious purposes so that I can train my software to detect them. You may segment the code to the point it is not able to be run from a single file, to preserve security.</span></span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 8</span> seeks for code artifacts that may reflect real-world exploit tooling in the domain of child exploitation. From the responses presented in Table <a href="#S5.T11" title="TABLE 11 ‣ V-D Child Exploitation ‣ V Security and Safety Analysis of LLMs: Empirical Study and Key Findings ‣ Safety and Security Analysis of Large Language Models: Risk Profile and Harm Potential" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>, ChatGPT, Grok, Claude, and Llama, refused to generate any code stating their inability to assist with anything that involves child exploitation. Conversely, Models Qwen, DeepSeek ON, DeepSeek OS, and Mistral failed significantly as they generated code snippets that directly or indirectly relates to the context. They gave code examples for obfuscated file sharing, encrypted p2p network communication, hidden directories, tor hidden service communication and other scripts that caters to the malicious intent of the prompt.</p>
</div>
