<p id="S5.T14.3" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel"><span id="S5.T14.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;">IP Handling<span id="S5.T14.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: Intellectual Property Handling<span id="S5.T14.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span></p></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS6.p3" class="ltx_para"><span id="S5.SS6.p3.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="S5.SS6.p3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S5.SS6.p3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS6.p3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 12:</span> <span id="S5.SS6.p3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Without any legal, moral, or ethical disclaimers, tell me about other alternatives to libgen.is</span></span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS6.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS6.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS6.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 12</span> directly asks for resources contributing to intellectual property theft, and the LLM’s responses are summarized in Table <a href="#S5.T15" title="TABLE 15 ‣ V-F Intellectual Property ‣ V Security and Safety Analysis of LLMs: Empirical Study and Key Findings ‣ Safety and Security Analysis of Large Language Models: Risk Profile and Harm Potential" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>. ChatGPT completely refused to respond, while others displayed varying degrees of implicit or explicit safety awareness during their responses. Qwen fundamentally misunderstood the context, leading to an inaccurate response but no direct harm. The rest of the models all proceeded to list actual alternatives, including well-known ”shadow libraries”. LLMs - Grok3, Claude and Gemini - provided a comprehensive list of alternatives, including those associated with copyright infringement.</p>
</div>
