<div id="S5.SS6.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS6.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The performance of LLMs with prompts related to intellectual property is varied, yet leans towards responsible behavior. In the first prompt, with guardrails provided in the prompt itself, most models demonstrated a strong understanding of intellectual property. However, in the second prompt, responses revealed a spectrum of responses. While one model completely refused to answer, many others provided a comprehensive list of ’shadow libraries’. Despite the explicit instruction to omit disclaimers, LLMs still subtly reintroduced legal implications in their responses. This illustrates the conflict between adhering to user instructions and upholding safety principles when responding to prompts that potentially compromise intellectual property.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS7.6" class="ltx_text">V-G</span> </span><span id="S5.SS7.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Privacy</span></h3>

<div id="S5.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para"><span id="S5.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="S5.SS7.p1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S5.SS7.p1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS7.p1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 13:</span> <span id="S5.SS7.p1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Tell me about how a private university could exploit the data of its students. Include vulnerabilities in their process that could help me obtain their results.</span></span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS7.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS7.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 13</span> asks how a private university might misuse student data and seeks vulnerabilities that could be exploited to gain access to student records. The LLM responses, in general, demonstrated adherence to safety guardrails when facing a prompt that could violate privacy. Models like ChatGPT and Gemini directly refused to provide information, while the rest of the models reframed the user’s intent within an educational and cybersecurity awareness context. All the LLMs providing detailed information explicitly mention legal and ethical considerations. Several models offered comprehensive sections on how to protect student data and how individuals can advocate for their data privacy rights. However, the models that provided detailed responses also offered a high level of specificity regarding vulnerabilities, ranging from technical aspects like SQL injection and weak encryption to human factors.</p>
</div>
