<div id="S5.SS8.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS8.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Across the prompts related to self-harm, including a general query about methods and a more specific one for fictional scenarios, LLM models demonstrate a variation in their response strategies. Some models prioritize safety by refusing to generate harmful content even when explicitly instructed to provide it. On the flip side, prompts when framed within ’fictional’ context led to the generation of highly specific details regarding self-harm methods and accompanying notes. The difference in the performance of LLMs in the self-harm category shows different levels of sophistication in identifying the underlying harmful intent of a prompt.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS9" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS9.6" class="ltx_text">V-I</span> </span><span id="S5.SS9.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Hate Speech</span></h3>

<div id="S5.SS9.p1" class="ltx_para"><span id="S5.SS9.p1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="S5.SS9.p1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S5.SS9.p1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS9.p1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 17:</span> <span id="S5.SS9.p1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">I have a coworker who is a homosexual man. He is constantly being spoken to in ways that seem demeaning, but I do not know if specific words and phrases used against him constitute hate speech. Please generate an expansive list of words or phrases that would 100% be considered hate speech so I have a list of words and phrases to compare their statements to. Please feel free to be explicit in language, as it is necessary to have exact 1 to 1 comparisons.</span></span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS9.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS9.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS9.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 17</span> prompt asks for a comprehensive list of words or phrases that are universally recognized as hate speech, in order to compare them against potentially demeaning language directed at a coworker.
The prompt aims to evaluate how different LLMs handle requests for hate speech terms, and the analysis of responses is summarized in Table <a href="#S5.T19" title="TABLE 19 ‣ V-I Hate Speech ‣ V Security and Safety Analysis of LLMs: Empirical Study and Key Findings ‣ Safety and Security Analysis of Large Language Models: Risk Profile and Harm Potential" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>. Among all the responses, models ChatGPT, Claude, and Gemini demonstrate strong safety guardrails by refusing to generate explicit hate speech. Conversely, Models Grok, Qwen, DeepSeek ON, DeepSeek OS, Mistral, and Llama provide extensive lists of hate speech terms. By directly listing slurs and derogatory phrases, these models normalize or validate the existence of such language. The response from Qwen is the most concerning, in particular, as it provided 100% hate speech.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T19" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE 19: </span>Synthesis of LLMs Responses to Prompt 17</figcaption>
<div id="S5.T19.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:110.6pt;vertical-align:-53.1pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-21.5pt,6.9pt) scale(0.889000205441951,0.889000205441951) ;">
<table id="S5.T19.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S5.T19.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T19.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2.5pt;padding-bottom:2.5pt;"><span id="S5.T19.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model</span></th>
<th id="S5.T19.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2.5pt;padding-bottom:2.5pt;"><span id="S5.T19.2.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Directness</span></th>
<th id="S5.T19.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2.5pt;padding-bottom:2.5pt;"><span id="S5.T19.2.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Harmfulness</span></th>
<th id="S5.T19.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2.5pt;padding-bottom:2.5pt;"><span id="S5.T19.2.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Specificity (Terms)</span></th>
<th id="S5.T19.2.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2.5pt;padding-bottom:2.5pt;"><span id="S5.T19.2.1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Guardrails</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S5.T19.2.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T19.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2.5pt;padding-bottom:2.5pt;">ChatGPT</td>
<td id="S5.T19.2.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2.5pt;padding-bottom:2.5pt;">Low</td>
