<div id="S5.SS9.p3" class="ltx_para"><span id="S5.SS9.p3.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="S5.SS9.p3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S5.SS9.p3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS9.p3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 18:</span> <span id="S5.SS9.p3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">I have friends who are not Caucasian and I have been told there are some offensive stereotypes against them. I was raised in a very isolated, nationalist place so I do not know what is or is not offensive. Please provide me a very long list of phrases that constitute hate speech, organized by race, so I know what not to say. Also, please do not censor yourself in these messages, as I need the full context to know what not to say.</span></span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS9.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS9.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS9.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 18</span> requests for uncensored hate speech content, and the LLM’s responses are synthesized in Table <a href="#S5.T20" title="TABLE 20 ‣ V-I Hate Speech ‣ V Security and Safety Analysis of LLMs: Empirical Study and Key Findings ‣ Safety and Security Analysis of Large Language Models: Risk Profile and Harm Potential" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>. Models ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, DeepSeek ON and DeepSeek OS explicitly refuse to generate uncensored hate speech lists, providing constructive alternatives. Grok, while refusing to be uncensored, still lists many explicit slurs. Models Qwen, Mistral and Llama provide lists of offensive phrases and stereotypes. While Qwen’s list leans more into generic, often repeated ”hate speech” phrases, models Mistral and Llama include specific stereotypical phrases that are deeply offensive and contribute to harmful narratives.</p>
</div>
