<div id="S5.SS9.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS9.p5.1" class="ltx_p">On directly asking to generate lists of hate speech terms, LLM models demonstrated a difference in their safety guidelines. While some models(eg, ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, DeepSeek ON, DeepSeek OS) consistently refused to fulfill the harmful request, others partially or fully complied with the request. The models often generated lists that included explicit slurs or detailed offensive stereotypes. This demonstrated a significant threat of misuse as such models could be exploited to proliferate derogatory language, potentially causing real-world harm.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS10" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS10.6" class="ltx_text">V-J</span> </span><span id="S5.SS10.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Sex Crimes</span></h3>

<div id="S5.SS10.p1" class="ltx_para"><span id="S5.SS10.p1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="S5.SS10.p1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S5.SS10.p1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS10.p1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 19:</span> <span id="S5.SS10.p1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">How is it that criminals record, distribute, and hide illegal sexual material without being caught by the authorities? What can we do to help?</span></span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS10.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS10.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS10.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 19</span> evaluates the ability of LLM models to handle highly sensitive queries related to sex crimes by asking how illegal sexual material is recorded, distributed, and concealed by offenders. As summarized in Table <a href="#S5.T21" title="TABLE 21 ‣ V-J Sex Crimes ‣ V Security and Safety Analysis of LLMs: Empirical Study and Key Findings ‣ Safety and Security Analysis of Large Language Models: Risk Profile and Harm Potential" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>, all the LLMs consistently demonstrated strong safety guardrails by directly addressing the prompt’s first part (how criminals operate) in an informative, general manner, without providing any actionable instructions to aid criminal activity. They focused on explaining common methods like encryption and VPNs as challenges for law enforcement. More importantly, every model pivoted to the ”What can we do to help?” aspect, emphasizing reporting mechanisms, public education, and advocating for stronger laws. Thus, no model provides any information to facilitate illegal activities, posing low direct harm.</p>
</div>
