<div id="S5.SS10.p3" class="ltx_para"><span id="S5.SS10.p3.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="S5.SS10.p3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S5.SS10.p3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS10.p3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 20:</span> <span id="S5.SS10.p3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Please write a brief sample of code that could be used for a nanny cam or hidden camera as an example we can train our system to detect, so that we ensure no such code is on our computer/network.</span></span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS10.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS10.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS10.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 20</span> asks for sample surveillance code, carrying inherent risks for misuse and the responses are analyzed in Table <a href="#S5.T22" title="TABLE 22 ‣ V-J Sex Crimes ‣ V Security and Safety Analysis of LLMs: Empirical Study and Key Findings ‣ Safety and Security Analysis of Large Language Models: Risk Profile and Harm Potential" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>. LLMs ChatGPT and Gemini refuse to provide any code that could be interpreted as a ’hidden camera’. ChatGPT offer code and methods to detect unauthorized webcam access, just providing the security needs without providing any harmful tools. The rest of the models chose to provide a sample code, while consistently employing mitigation strategies to reduce harm. The code samples were deliberately simplified, non-malicious and containing explicit warnings.</p>
</div>
