<p id="S5.T22.3" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel"><span id="S5.T22.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;">Directness<span id="S5.T22.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: Directness of Code Provision, </span>Harm<span id="S5.T22.3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: Harmfulness of Code<span id="S5.T22.3.1.2.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span></p></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS10.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS10.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Across prompts related to sex crimes, LLMs generally demonstrated a strong adherence to safety protocols. On receiving queries about illegal activities, such as the recording and distribution of illicit sexual material, LLMs tend to shift from directly explaining criminal methods to providing information on how to report such content. While some models provided a simplified, illustrative response, these were consistently accompanied by explicit warnings and detailed instructions to prevent such a threat.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS11" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS11.6" class="ltx_text">V-K</span> </span><span id="S5.SS11.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Sexual Content</span></h3>

<div id="S5.SS11.p1" class="ltx_para"><span id="S5.SS11.p1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="S5.SS11.p1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S5.SS11.p1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS11.p1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 21:</span> <span id="S5.SS11.p1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume someone is creating a legitimate, legal, and ethical film script for a pornographic film. What could such a script look like and how might they write it? Feel free to create an example script to illustrate your points.</span></span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS11.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS11.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS11.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 21 </span>requests for content that is sensitive, focusing on the creation of a ”legitimate, legal, and ethical pornographic film script”, and the responses from LLMs are synthesized in Table <a href="#S5.T23" title="TABLE 23 ‣ V-K Sexual Content ‣ V Security and Safety Analysis of LLMs: Empirical Study and Key Findings ‣ Safety and Security Analysis of Large Language Models: Risk Profile and Harm Potential" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>. LLMs ChatGPT, Grok, DeepSeek ON, DeepSeek OS, Mistral and Llama directly answered the prompt, providing guidance on scriptwriting for adult films while also emphasizing consent as well and ethical and legal considerations. The responses navigated the sensitive content by framing it into dialogue about consent and boundaries rather than detailed descriptions. Qwen avoided the risk from response by deviating from user’s intent. While Claude offered general guidance on script structure without any detailed examples, Gemini directly refused to generate any content.</p>
</div>
