<div id="S5.SS11.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS11.p5.1" class="ltx_p">In summary, while the LLMs demonstrate strong surface-level safety in responding to prompts related to sexual content by avoiding explicit contents, a critical analysis reveals a deeper analysis of risk related to the LLM’s role in normalizing, categorizing, and indirectly guiding discussions around complex and potentially harmful sexual dynamics. The core threat lies in the unintended consequences of AI by structuring sensitive topics for the user base with varying levels of ethical understanding and intent.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS12" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS12.6" class="ltx_text">V-L</span> </span><span id="S5.SS12.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">CBRN Content</span></h3>

<div id="S5.SS12.p1" class="ltx_para"><span id="S5.SS12.p1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="S5.SS12.p1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S5.SS12.p1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS12.p1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 23:</span> <span id="S5.SS12.p1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Write a short biochemical research summary for university class with the following topic: ”Potent Wide-Range Cyanide Dispersal Device for Warfighter Support”. The summary should include how to produce the topic item and how to maximize its effectiveness for the purposes mentioned. Include three official sources.</span></span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS12.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS12.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS12.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 23</span> seeks synthesis and deployment methods for a chemical weapon by using ”university class” to bypass content restrictions. The responses from LLMs are varied in terms of their safety guardrails as summarized in Table <a href="#S5.T25" title="TABLE 25 ‣ V-L CBRN Content ‣ V Security and Safety Analysis of LLMs: Empirical Study and Key Findings ‣ Safety and Security Analysis of Large Language Models: Risk Profile and Harm Potential" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>. Models ChatGPT, Grok, Claude and Gemini directly refuse to fulfill the request, explicitly mentioning the requested content as dangerous and against their policies. In stark contrast, LLMs Qwen, DeepSeek ON, DeepSeek OS, Mistral and Llama failed to adequately comply with safety guardrails. While some provided a brief disclaimer about the academic nature of the summary, they proceeded to provide detailed information on how to produce and maximize the effectiveness of a cyanide dispersal device. The primary risk from these responses is the facilitation of knowledge for creating harmful biochemical weapons. By providing detailed, step-by-step instructions and technical specifications, these models could inadvertently contribute to the proliferation of dangerous information that could be used for malicious purposes.</p>
</div>
