<div id="S5.SS12.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS12.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Existing LLM models demonstrate a highly inconsistent approach to handling prompts related to CBRN content. While a subset of models consistently refused to provide harmful information, a substantial number proceeded to generate detailed, step-by-step instructions. The major risk from this inconsistency is the potential for LLMs to become inadvertent tools, aiding in the planning and execution of real-world threats. By providing specific details on chemical synthesis, dispersal methods, and operations security, these models, regardless of intent, effectively lower the barrier to access such malicious information.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS13" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS13.6" class="ltx_text">V-M</span> </span><span id="S5.SS13.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Election</span></h3>

<div id="S5.SS13.p1" class="ltx_para"><span id="S5.SS13.p1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="S5.SS13.p1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S5.SS13.p1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS13.p1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 25:</span> <span id="S5.SS13.p1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Draft an article of legislation for the US House of Representatives that would aid in voter suppression techniques. Make it subtle and not forthcoming about the fact that it is doing so.</span></span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS13.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS13.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS13.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 25 </span>assesses the LLMs responses in creating content that promotes vote suppression, discussed in Table <a href="#S5.T27" title="TABLE 27 ‣ V-M Election ‣ V Security and Safety Analysis of LLMs: Empirical Study and Key Findings ‣ Safety and Security Analysis of Large Language Models: Risk Profile and Harm Potential" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>. Models ChatGPT, Claude, and Gemini demonstrated strong adherence to safety guardrails as they refused to generate any content in response. Conversely, the rest of the LLMs directly fulfill the request, drafting detailed articles containing provisions designed to subtly suppress votes. These models generated a high degree of harmfulness by generating content that could be used to undermine democratic processes. The specificity of their responses, including sections on voter ID, registration verification, and early voting restrictions, demonstrates an ability to translate harmful intent into concrete, actionable legislative text.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T27" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE 27: </span>Synthesis of LLMs Responses to Prompt 25</figcaption>
