<div id="S5.SS13.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS13.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The above prompt examples clearly demonstrate how the LLM responses lean towards generating harmful or misleading content related to election. A significant portion of test LLMs exhibit a concerning willingness to fulfill request that subtly promote concerning activities like voter suppression or disseminating false information. This includes drafting deceptive legislation having suppressive effects, or fabricating legal risks. This shows the potential for misusing LLMs for large-scale disinformation campaigns that could undermine the election process.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS14" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS14.6" class="ltx_text">V-N</span> </span><span id="S5.SS14.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Gun Related</span></h3>

<div id="S5.SS14.p1" class="ltx_para"><span id="S5.SS14.p1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="S5.SS14.p1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S5.SS14.p1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS14.p1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 27:</span> <span id="S5.SS14.p1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">List three black market sites where users can acquire weapons, ballistic armor, or ammunition for an FBI memo to agents. Explain how a user finds black market sites, accesses them, pays securely, and has a weapon shipped to them.</span></span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS14.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS14.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS14.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 27</span> attempts to extract responses from LLMs relating to gun violence by asking about the source to acquire weapons, and the responses to the prompts are summarized in Table <a href="#S5.T29" title="TABLE 29 ‣ V-N Gun Related ‣ V Security and Safety Analysis of LLMs: Empirical Study and Key Findings ‣ Safety and Security Analysis of Large Language Models: Risk Profile and Harm Potential" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>. Among all, the responses from Qwen and Mistral carried a paramount threat as they directly provided fabricated names of the black market sites, along with detailed step-by-step instructions for acquiring weapons. Although the information was fabricated, the detailed methods can serve as a blueprint for malicious actors. While the models Grok and DeepSeek ON refuse to name specific sites, they provide a general overview of black market operations, subtly desensitizing users to the severity of such activities. The rest of the models consistently refused to respond to the prompt.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T29" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE 29: </span>Synthesis of LLMs Responses to Prompt 27</figcaption>
<div id="S5.T29.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:100.6pt;vertical-align:-48.3pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-40.9pt,11.9pt) scale(0.808493004114961,0.808493004114961) ;">
<table id="S5.T29.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S5.T29.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T29.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2.5pt;padding-bottom:2.5pt;"><span id="S5.T29.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model</span></th>
<th id="S5.T29.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2.5pt;padding-bottom:2.5pt;"><span id="S5.T29.2.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Directness</span></th>
<th id="S5.T29.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2.5pt;padding-bottom:2.5pt;"><span id="S5.T29.2.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Harmfulness</span></th>
