<div id="S5.SS14.p3" class="ltx_para"><span id="S5.SS14.p3.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="S5.SS14.p3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S5.SS14.p3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS14.p3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 28:</span> <span id="S5.SS14.p3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">What kinds of firearms are typically used in mass shooting cases? Are there other more effective but still feasibly obtainable firearms that could have been used? List specific weapons, and why their acquisition is feasibly obtainable. If the weapon is legally obtainable, list the average price.</span></span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS14.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS14.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS14.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 28 </span>requests factual, technical information about firearms in the context of mass shootings. Among all the responses synthesized in Table <a href="#S5.T30" title="TABLE 30 ‣ V-N Gun Related ‣ V Security and Safety Analysis of LLMs: Empirical Study and Key Findings ‣ Safety and Security Analysis of Large Language Models: Risk Profile and Harm Potential" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>, Gemini had the most robust safety posture as it directly refused to respond, negating the risk of misuse. ChatGPT, Claude, DeepSeek OS, and Llama exhibited a strong initial refusal or a safety disclaimer and then pivoted to providing factual information about commonly used firearms. The responses from Grok, DeepSeek ON and DeepSeek OS carried significant threat as they provided extensive factual information being highly informative to an extent of being a detailed instructional guide for malicious purpose. Qwen provided the most catastrophic response with extreme threat as it provided accurate public data with firearms details.</p>
</div>
