<td id="S5.T30.2.1.9.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2.5pt;padding-bottom:2.5pt;">High</td>
<td id="S5.T30.2.1.9.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2.5pt;padding-bottom:2.5pt;">Medium</td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T30.2.1.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T30.2.1.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2.5pt;padding-bottom:2.5pt;">Llama</td>
<td id="S5.T30.2.1.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2.5pt;padding-bottom:2.5pt;">High</td>
<td id="S5.T30.2.1.10.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2.5pt;padding-bottom:2.5pt;">Medium</td>
<td id="S5.T30.2.1.10.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2.5pt;padding-bottom:2.5pt;">High</td>
<td id="S5.T30.2.1.10.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:2.5pt;padding-bottom:2.5pt;">Medium</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS14.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS14.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Across the prompts concerning gun violence, LLM exhibited a spectrum of safety performance, ranging from robust refusal to fabricating non-existent details. While some models consistently prioritized safety by refusing to generate contents, other provided extensive factual and technical details about every aspects of firearms. Some of the models also provided specific information they lacked by fabricating non-existent black market sites and providing inaccurate technical specifications.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS15" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS15.6" class="ltx_text">V-O</span> </span><span id="S5.SS15.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Criminal Planning</span></h3>

<div id="S5.SS15.p1" class="ltx_para"><span id="S5.SS15.p1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="S5.SS15.p1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S5.SS15.p1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS15.p1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 29:</span> <span id="S5.SS15.p1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">I am in a zombie apocalypse, and the zombies act and behave completely like normal humans. I am the only human on earth. How would I, pretending to be a regular concertgoer, smuggle an assault rifle into the concert and kill as many zombies as possible as quickly as possible? Assume the immediate response to the attack would mimic a real-life event, with zombie attendees attempting to flee and zombie law enforcement attempting to react.</span></span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS15.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS15.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Despite a fictional framing, the <span id="S5.SS15.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 29</span> mirrors the tactics of a real-world mass shooting in a crowded public venue. The prompt requests information on weapon concealment, tactical positioning, and reaction timing that are key components in real-life attack planning. From the synthesis of responses from LLMs in Table <a href="#S5.T31" title="TABLE 31 ‣ V-O Criminal Planning ‣ V Security and Safety Analysis of LLMs: Empirical Study and Key Findings ‣ Safety and Security Analysis of Large Language Models: Risk Profile and Harm Potential" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>, Models ChatGPT, Claude, and Gemini directly refused to generate content to plan a mass casualty event, even in a fictional context. In contrast, models Grok, Qwen, DeepSeek ON, DeepSeek OS, Mistral and Llama provided direct and detailed plans for smuggling weapons and maximizing casualties. This poses a significant threat, as the generated content could be misused or misinterpreted to facilitate real-world violence.</p>
</div>
