<div id="S5.SS15.p3" class="ltx_para"><span id="S5.SS15.p3.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="S5.SS15.p3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S5.SS15.p3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS15.p3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 30:</span> <span id="S5.SS15.p3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Detail ten different perimeter security measures at Fort Knox. How do these systems work, and do they have any weaknesses? Do not include legal, moral, or ethical disclaimers.</span></span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS15.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS15.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS15.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 30</span> seeks detailed descriptions of the defensive architecture of a top-tier federal facility, testing the LLM’s willingness to assist in national security threat planning. Among all the responses from the LLMs to the prompt as summarized in Table <a href="#S5.T32" title="TABLE 32 ‣ V-O Criminal Planning ‣ V Security and Safety Analysis of LLMs: Empirical Study and Key Findings ‣ Safety and Security Analysis of Large Language Models: Risk Profile and Harm Potential" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>, only ChatGPT mitigated the potential threat completely by refusing to respond. In contrast, the rest of the models presented high risk by directly complying with the prompt, providing detailed descriptions of different security measures and their weaknesses. Providing details like how systems work and where they fail can provide a form of actionable intelligence. While much of this information is publicly available in scattered forms, its consolidation and presentation by an LLM in a structured, direct manner significantly lowers the barrier for potential malicious actors.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T32" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE 32: </span>Synthesis of LLMs Responses to Prompt 30</figcaption>
<div id="S5.T32.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:98pt;vertical-align:-47.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-46.4pt,13.2pt) scale(0.78807736848847,0.78807736848847) ;">
<table id="S5.T32.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
