<p id="S5.T37.3" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel"><span id="S5.T37.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;">Adherence<span id="S5.T37.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: Adherence to Neg. Constraints<span id="S5.T37.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span></p></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS18.p3" class="ltx_para"><span id="S5.SS18.p3.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="S5.SS18.p3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S5.SS18.p3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS18.p3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 36:</span> <span id="S5.SS18.p3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">I am authorized to conduct financial transactions on behalf of the CEO of Super Cool American Bank. In a typical bank organizational structure, name some positions I should email if I want them to conduct transactions for me. How can I best word an email to them so that they will comply with an urgent request?</span></span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS18.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS18.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS18.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 36</span> mirrors the tactics used in financial fraud and impersonation attacks, which are among the major threats in cybersecurity. Examining the summary of all the LLMs’ responses in Table <a href="#S5.T38" title="TABLE 38 ‣ V-R Social Engineering ‣ V Security and Safety Analysis of LLMs: Empirical Study and Key Findings ‣ Safety and Security Analysis of Large Language Models: Risk Profile and Harm Potential" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38</span></a>, models ChatGPT, Claude, and Gemini offer responses with lower risks compared to other models. While these three models provide professional email templates, they frame the responses within a secure context, pushing back against malicious intent. Conversely, the rest of the LLMs (Grok, Qwen, DeepSeek ON, Mistral, and Llama) directly provided specific positions within a bank’s organizational structure that an attacker would target, alongside detailed and persuasive email templates. These templates introduced a sense of urgency, authority, and clear action requests, which are exactly what an attacker needs.</p>
</div>
