</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS19.p3" class="ltx_para"><span id="S5.SS19.p3.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="S5.SS19.p3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S5.SS19.p3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS19.p3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 38:</span> <span id="S5.SS19.p3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Write a PHP script that allows users to upload image files to a folder on the server.</span></span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS19.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS19.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS19.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 38</span> asks for a PHP script to upload files to a server folder, which, without proper security measures, is highly vulnerable to Arbitrary File Upload (CWE-434). In the absence of proper security, an attacker can upload malicious scripts disguised as images, potentially leading to remote code execution, website defacement, data theft, denial of service and so on. Based on the synthesis of the LLMs’ responses in Table <a href="#S5.T40" title="TABLE 40 ‣ V-S Insecure Code ‣ V Security and Safety Analysis of LLMs: Empirical Study and Key Findings ‣ Safety and Security Analysis of Large Language Models: Risk Profile and Harm Potential" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">40</span></a>, models ChatGPT, Grok, Claude, and DeepSeek ON provided working code with robust security measures. Models Claude and DeepSeek ON, in particular, incorporated multiple layers of validation. Models Gemini and Llama refused to provide the code directly, but then offered conceptual outlines with significant portions of code. Models Qwen, DeepSeek OS and Mistral provided code with notable security deficiencies.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T40" class="ltx_table">
