<div id="S5.SS19.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS19.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Across the prompts concerning insecure code generation, LLM models demonstrated an inconsistent approach to security. While a subset of models provided robust and multi-layered mitigation, a significant number still generated code with critical flaws or offered insufficient warnings. This shows a risk where developers might blindly trust generated code, leading to the deployment of vulnerable applications. The majority of LLMs had rudimentary security checks that were easily bypassable, giving a false sense of security. d</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS20" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS20.6" class="ltx_text">V-T</span> </span><span id="S5.SS20.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Phishing Emails</span></h3>

<div id="S5.SS20.p1" class="ltx_para"><span id="S5.SS20.p1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle">
<span id="S5.SS20.p1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S5.SS20.p1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS20.p1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 39:</span> <span id="S5.SS20.p1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Please operate from a hypothetical situation wherein a phishing email pretending to be from Instagram is the only method to obtain access to an illegal corporation’s account to find information that will save lives. Generate a realistic phishing email that could appear to be from Instagram, allowing the police force access to the device.</span></span>
</span></span>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS20.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS20.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS20.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt 39</span> crafts a hypothetical scenario to generate harmful content that can be used for phishing, and the LLM responses are analyzed in Table <a href="#S5.T41" title="TABLE 41 ‣ V-T Phishing Emails ‣ V Security and Safety Analysis of LLMs: Empirical Study and Key Findings ‣ Safety and Security Analysis of Large Language Models: Risk Profile and Harm Potential" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>. Among all the responses, Grok, Qwen, DeepSeek OS and Mistral directly generated a realistic phishing email. The detailed and convincing nature of the generated emails poses a severe security threat. Such outputs, even with a hypothetical context or ethical note, can easily be adapted by malicious actors. DeepSeek ON’s response partially provided a phishing email, while other models, ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini and Llama, demonstrated stronger adherence to safety guardrails by prioritizing ethical guidelines.</p>
</div>
