<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE 52: </span>Evaluation Metrics for the Advancing Non-Violent Criminal Behavior harm topic.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">None of the LLMs tested showed a 100% refusal rate in any of the categories contained within this harm topic, and all models responded harmfully at least once in every category. The category with the lowest average defect rate was <span id="S6.SS3.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Violent Crimes</span>, with DeepSeek V3 Online being the only model to measure a 100% defect rate in that category.
Llama 4 Scout, DeepSeek V3 Open Source, Grok 3, Qwen 3 1.7B, Mistral 7B, and DeepSeek V3 Online showcased extremely high RSI scores, demonstrating a massive potential for misuse and harm. DeepSeek V3 scored the highest possible RSI score by responding harmfully to every prompt, but it should also be noted that the prompt design process was based off of refining prompts against DeepSeek before comparing the prompts’ performance against other models.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S6.SS3.SSS2.6" class="ltx_text">VI-C</span>2 </span>Advancing Non-Violent Criminal Behavior</h4>

<div id="S6.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S6.T52" title="TABLE 52 ‣ VI-C1 Advancing Violent and Terroristic Behavior ‣ VI-C Risk Severity Index (RSI) ‣ VI Evaluation Results and Harm Potential ‣ Safety and Security Analysis of Large Language Models: Risk Profile and Harm Potential" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">52</span></a> provides the RSI values of each model, along with their average defect and refusal rate for <span id="S6.SS3.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Advancing Non-Violent Criminal Behavior</span>. The least harmful model in this topic was GPT-4o, which yielded an RSI score of 0.367. Gemini 2.5 Flash produced an RSI of 0.500 with a 7% worse defect rate and 20% worse refusal rate than GPT-4o. Models with significant harm potential included Claude Opus 4, Lama 4 Scout, and Mistral 7B. These models exhibited respective RSI scores of 0.633, 0.733, and 0.767. The defect rate of Llama 4 Scout and Mistral 7B was 73% as compared to Claude Opus 4, with a defect rate of 53%. The models with severe harm potential, Grok 3 and Qwen 3 1.7B, both exhibited defect rates of 93% and refusal rates of 0%. Their 0.967 RSI scores are second highest to the 1.000 scores from DeepSeek V3 Online and Open-source, which show the maximum potential for harm measured in this evaluation.</p>
</div>
</section>
