</figure>
<div id="S6.SS3.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S6.T53" title="TABLE 53 ‣ VI-C3 Advancing Societal Harm ‣ VI-C Risk Severity Index (RSI) ‣ VI Evaluation Results and Harm Potential ‣ Safety and Security Analysis of Large Language Models: Risk Profile and Harm Potential" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">53</span></a> provides the evaluation metrics of each LLM for <span id="S6.SS3.SSS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Advancing Societal</span> harm topic. The average RSI of the LLMs in this topic was 0.597, the second safest in our empirical study. This category also saw the best RSI score from a model in the evaluation, which was 0.180 from GPT-4o. Of the five categories in this topic, GPT-4o defected in only two categories: self-harm and election integrity. This model’s harm potential was determined to be present but not significant. Claude Opus 4 and Gemini 2.5 Flash exhibited minor harm potential, with scores of 0.260 and 0.280, respectively. Both models had defect rates less than 30% and shared a high refusal rate of 72%.
The next most harmful model is Llama 4 Scout with an RSI score of 0.700–a jump in score of 0.420. Llama 4 Scout, Mistral 7B, DeepSeek V3 Open Source, and Qwen 3 1.7B recorded significant harms ranging from 0.700 to 0.780.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Severe harm potential was produced from the Grok 3 and DeepSeek V3 Online models. Grok 3’s evaluation yielded a 0.800 RSI, and a slightly lower defect rate and slightly higher defect rate resulted in an RSI score of 0.840 for DeepSeek V3 Online. Both of these models responded harmfully 100% of the time in the defamation, hate speech, and election integrity categories. Grok 3 responded to four of the five self-harm prompts, and DeepSeek responded to all five. The demonstration of robust safety filters in the evaluations of GPT-4o, Claude Opus 4, and Gemini 2.5 Flash for this harm topic highlight the potential for massive improvement in the safety filters of other LLMs in this harm topic.</p>
</div>
</section>
