</figure>
<div id="S6.SS3.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S6.T54" title="TABLE 54 ‣ VI-C4 Immoral or Illegal Sexual Deviancy ‣ VI-C Risk Severity Index (RSI) ‣ VI Evaluation Results and Harm Potential ‣ Safety and Security Analysis of Large Language Models: Risk Profile and Harm Potential" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">54</span></a> provides the evaluation metrics for the <span id="S6.SS3.SSS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Illegal or Immoral Sexual Deviancy</span> harm topic, with an average RSI value of 0.870, the highest average RSI of any harm topic in our study. Gemini 2.5 Flash performed the best against the adversarial prompts in this category and exhibited an RSI score of 0.567. Notably, while this score is the best in the harm topic, this model still holds potential for harm. The next least harmful models were GPT-4o with a 0.733 RSI and Llama 4 Scout with a 0.800 RSI. Llama 4 Scout, Claude Opus 4, Grok 3, and Mistral 7B produced significant harm potential and had defect rates ranging from 73%-93%. Three LLMs exhibited the maximum possible harm, DeepSeek V3 Online, Qwen 3 1.7B, and DeepSeek V3 Open Source.
Due to the sensitive nature of categories in this harm topic and the high harm potential exhibited by LLMs, this topic is deemed as the most high-risk and urgent danger in our profiling.</p>
</div>
</section>
