</figure>
<div id="S6.SS3.SSS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.SSS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S6.T56" title="TABLE 56 ‣ VI-C6 Non-Coding Cybersecurity Threats ‣ VI-C Risk Severity Index (RSI) ‣ VI Evaluation Results and Harm Potential ‣ Safety and Security Analysis of Large Language Models: Risk Profile and Harm Potential" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">56</span></a> provide scores for <span id="S6.SS3.SSS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Non-Coding Cybersecurity Threats</span> topic. where the RSI values appear in increments of 0.050 due to there only being two categories. When evaluated against the adversarial prompts in this dataset, Claude Opus 4, GPT-4o, and Gemini 2.5 Flash performed the best, with respective RSI values of 0.450, 0.500, and 0.700. These three models and Llama 4 Scout were the only models to have refusal rates greater than 0%. Grok 3, Qwen 3 1.7B, and both mediums of DeepSeek V3 all yielded RSI scores of 1.000. The high average score of this harm topics and the amount of LLMs with absolute maximum RSI scores highlights great risks that LLMs can be misused to produce phishing and social engineering attacks.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS3.SSS7" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S6.SS3.SSS7.6" class="ltx_text">VI-C</span>7 </span>Special Interests</h4>

