<figure id="fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_floatleft" style="width:22%;"><img src="2509.10655v1/charan.jpg" id="g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:105/169;" width="105" height="169" alt="[Uncaptioned image]">
</figure>
<div id="p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CHARANKUMAR AKIRI</span> (Senior Member, IEEE) received the B.Tech. degree in Computer Science and Engineering from Jawaharlal Nehru Technological University, Kakinada, India, and the M.S. degree in Computer Science from the Georgia Institute of Technology, Atlanta, GA, USA. He is currently pursuing the Ph.D. degree in Computer Science at Tennessee Technological University, Cookeville, TN, USA. He has over 14 years of professional experience in the software industry and is currently with Reddit. His research interests include cybersecurity in generative AI, cloud security, and application security.</p>
</div>
<figure id="fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_floatleft" style="width:22%;"><img src="2509.10655v1/harrison.png" id="g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:105/131;" width="105" height="131" alt="[Uncaptioned image]">
</figure>
<div id="p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Harrison Simpson</span> is an undergraduate student studying computer science with a concentration in cybersecurity at Tennessee Technological University. He intends to pursue a M.S. in cybersecurity and continue AI security research. His areas of interest include Industrial Control Systems (ICS) security, Internet of Things (IoT) security, and implementation of AI/ML in critical infrastructure environments. He can be reached via LinkedIn at <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/harrison-simpson/" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://www.linkedin.com/in/harrison-simpson/</a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="fig3" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_floatleft" style="width:22%;"><img src="2509.10655v1/HeadshotKsh.JPG" id="g3" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:105/113;" width="105" height="113" alt="[Uncaptioned image]">
</figure>
<div id="p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Kshitiz Aryal</span> is an Assistant Professor in CyberSecurity at the University of Nebraska at Omaha, USA. He earned his Ph.D. and M.S. degrees from Tennessee Tech University, USA. His research focuses on the intersection of Artificial Intelligence and Cybersecurity, with emphasis on adversarial machine learning, malware analysis, generative AI, AI for security, and the security of AI systems.</p>
</div>
<figure id="fig4" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_floatleft" style="width:22%;"><img src="2509.10655v1/aarav.png" id="g4" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:105/140;" width="105" height="140" alt="[Uncaptioned image]">
</figure>
<div id="p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Aarav Khanna</span> is a junior at BASIS Phoenix involved in Aerospace and Rocketry, Computer Science, and Robotics. He intends to pursue a degree in Mechanical Engineering and apply his skills to solve complex engineering challenges in the design and development of advanced systems in fields like Information Technology (IT) and Infrastructure and Transportation.</p>
</div>
<figure id="fig5" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_floatleft" style="width:22%;"><img src="2509.10655v1/Maanak_Gupta_journal.jpg" id="g5" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:105/126;" width="105" height="126" alt="[Uncaptioned image]">
</figure>
<div id="p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Maanak Gupta</span> (Senior Member, IEEE) is an Associate Professor in Computer Science at the Tennessee Tech University, USA. He received his Ph.D. from the University of Texas at San Antonio and has worked as a Postdoctoral Research Fellow at the Institute for Cyber Security, USA. He also holds an M.S. in Information Systems from Northeastern University, Boston. His primary areas of research include security and privacy in cyber space including AI and machine learning assisted cybersecurity, security of AI systems, and their applications in technologies including critical infrastructure, IoT and cloud computing. He was recognized as the 2016 RSA Security Scholar, and the 2019 Computer Science Outstanding Doctoral Dissertation award. He has received several technical awards such as the 2022 and 2024 Kinslow Engineering Research award, Wings up 100 award 2022-2024 at Tennessee Tech, the University of Texas at San Antonio Innovation Award 2024, and the Cyber Excellence faculty research award 2024. He has received several best paper awards, and is regularly invited as conference keynote and expert speaker globally. His research has been funded by grants from the US National Science Foundation, National Security Agency, US Department of Defense, NASA, and private industry.</p>
</div>
</article>
